/*
 * /privacy — the Privacy Policy.
 *
 * EVERY DATA CLAIM BELOW WAS READ OUT OF THE SCHEMA AND THE AUTH CODE, NOT ASSUMED. A
 * privacy policy that describes a plausible product rather than this one is worse than none:
 * it is a published, signed statement that is false. Sources, so the next person can re-check
 * rather than re-derive:
 *
 *   WHAT WE GET FROM GITHUB
 *     src/cloud/auth.ts:214            provider=github, PKCE, loopback callback
 *     supabase/functions/command/index.ts:1188-1206
 *                                      user id + email; display name is the first non-empty
 *                                      of GitHub full_name, name, user_name, then the local
 *                                      part of the email, then the literal "Coswarm User"
 *     :3205 (identityVerified)         derived from Supabase's email_confirmed_at
 *
 *   WHERE IT LANDS
 *     migrations/20260723000001_p1_schema.sql:111   swarm.users (user_id, display_name,
 *                                                   created_at)
 *     migrations/20260724000001_connect_loop.sql:5  + email, added later, and the column
 *                                                   comment says outright it is bookkeeping
 *                                                   only and never an authorization input
 *     :117 devices  :127 workspaces  :135 memberships  :149 invitations
 *     :174 agent_principals  :184 agent_runs  :192 agent_tokens
 *     :281 events (payload capped at 65536 bytes)  :309 tasks  :384 audit_log
 *     migrations/20260724000003_signals.sql:3      signals (body 1-2000, about <= 500,
 *                                                  until <= 30 days)
 *
 *   THE IP CLAIM IS THE ONE WORTH RE-CHECKING BEFORE ANY EDIT.
 *     swarm.audit_log HAS an `ip inet` column (p1_schema.sql:400), and the edge function
 *     names it in the INSERT column list — then writes a literal NULL into it
 *     (supabase/functions/command/index.ts:676, :691). So the honest statement is "the
 *     column exists and we do not write to it", which is what the document says. If anyone
 *     ever populates it, THIS DOCUMENT IS WRONG THAT DAY. Do not restate the claim from
 *     memory; re-read insertAudit.
 *
 *   THE WEBSITE HAS NO ANALYTICS AND NO COOKIES. Checked across site/src, site/package.json
 *     and site/astro.config.mjs: no gtag, plausible, posthog, segment, @vercel/analytics or
 *     speed-insights, and the only dependency is astro. Fonts are self-hosted woff2 in
 *     site/public/fonts (global.css @font-face), so a page load makes no third-party
 *     request. SiteFooter already states "no tracking on this page" in rendered markup —
 *     this document has to stay true to that or one of the two is a lie.
 *
 *   WHAT WE DO *NOT* TOUCH, and the document says so because a reader assumes otherwise:
 *     no repository contents. swarm.github_installations and swarm.repositories exist in the
 *     schema, but no repo-mapping command is exposed — COMMAND_KINDS
 *     (supabase/functions/command/index.ts:331) is create, acquire, renew, handoff, takeover,
 *     submit, close, reopen, invite_member, accept_invitation, create_agent_principal,
 *     mint_agent_token, post_signal. Nothing reads code.
 *
 * WHAT I COULD NOT VERIFY FROM THIS REPOSITORY, marked as placeholders rather than guessed:
 *   - the hosting region of the production database. supabase/config.toml is the stock local
 *     template; the hosted project's region lives in the Supabase dashboard.
 *   - the exact OAuth scopes requested from GitHub. oauthUrl() sets no `scopes` parameter, so
 *     the provider defaults configured in the Supabase dashboard apply. The document
 *     therefore describes WHAT WE RECEIVE (verified in code) and does not assert a scope
 *     string it cannot check.
 *
 * NOTES GO IN THIS BLOCK, NEVER IN THE MARKUP — Astro ships <!-- comments --> verbatim.
 */

